hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
1,"Ibn `Umar narrated that:the Prophet said: \Salat will not be accepted without purification"""
2,
3,"# Translation of the Hadith\n\n**Qutaybah, Hannād, and Maḥmūd ibn Ghaylān** narrated to us, who said: **Wakīʿ** narrated to us, from **Sufyān**. And **Muḥammad ibn Bashshār** narrated to us, who said: **ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī** narrated to us, who said: **Sufyān** narrated to us, from **ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAqīl**, from **Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥanafiyyah**, from **ʿAlī** (may Allāh be pleased with him), from the Prophet ﷺ, who said:\n\n> **\The key to prayer is purification", its consecration is the takbīr (saying 'Allāhu Akbar')," and its dissolution is the taslīm (saying the salām).\""**\n\n**Abū ʿĪsā** (al-Tirmidhī) said: *\""This hadith is the most authentic and the best narration on this topic.\""*\n\n**ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAqīl** is **ṣadūq** (truthful)"," although some of the scholars of hadith have spoken regarding him on account of his memory.\n\n**Abū ʿĪsā** said: *\""I heard Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl (al-Bukhārī) say: 'Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal", Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm," and al-Ḥumaydī used to cite the narrations of ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAqīl as evidence.'\""*\n\n**Muḥammad** (ibn Ismāʿīl al-Bukhārī) said: *\""He is muqārib al-ḥadīth (of acceptable narrations).\""*\n\n**Abū ʿĪsā** said: *\""And in this chapter there are narrations from Jābir and Abū Saʿīd (may Allāh be pleased with them).\""*"""
4,"Narrated to us by Abū Bakr, Muḥammad ibn Zanjawayh al-Baghdādī and others, who said: narrated to us al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad, narrated to us Sulaymān ibn Qarm, from Abū Yaḥyā al-Qattāt, from Mujāhid, from Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh (may Allāh be pleased with them both), who said: the Messenger of Allāh, peace and blessings be upon him, said:\n\n\The key to Paradise is prayer (ṣalāh)"," and the key to prayer is ablution (wuḍūʾ).\"""""
5,"Anas bin Malik said:\When the Prophet entered the toilet he would say: 'O Allah Indeed I seek refuge in You.'\"" Shu'bah (one of the narrators) said: \""Another time he said: 'I seek refuge in You from AI-Khubthi and al-Khablth.' Or: 'Al-Khubthi and Al-Khaba'ith"""
6,"Anas bin Malik said:\When the Prophet would enter the toilet 'He said: \""O Allah! Indeed I seek refuge in You from Al-Khubith and Al- Khaba'ith"""
7,"Narrated by Muhammad ibn Isma'il, from Malik ibn Isma'il, from Isra'il ibn Yunus, from Yusuf ibn Abi Burdah, from his father, from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), who said:\n\n\The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) would say upon exiting the privy: *'Ghufrānaka'* (I seek Your forgiveness).\""\n\nAbu Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: \""This is a *hasan gharib* hadith. We do not know it except through the narration of Isra'il from Yusuf ibn Abi Burdah. And Abu Burdah ibn Abi Musa's name is Amir ibn Abdullah ibn Qays al-Ash'ari. And we do not know of any other hadith in this chapter except the hadith of Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him).\"""""
8,"Abu Ayyub Al-Ansari narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: \When one of you arrives to defecate"""
9,"Jabir bin Abdullah said:\The Prophet prohibited us from facing the Qiblah while urinating. Then i saw him facing it a year before he died"""
10,Abu Qatadah narrated that :he saw the Prophet urinating while facing the Qiblah. Qutaibah narrated that to us
11,Narrated by Ibn ʿUmar (may Allāh be pleased with him): \n\I once climbed upon the roof of Ḥafṣah’s house and saw the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) answering the call of nature," facing Syria and turning his back toward the Kaʿbah.\""\n\nAbū ʿĪsā (may Allāh have mercy on him) said: \""This is a ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ hadith.\"""""
12,"Aishah said:\Whoever narrated to you that the Prophet would urinate while standing; then do not believe him. He would not urinate except while squatting.\"" [He said:] There are narrations on this topic from Umar"""
13,"Hudhaifah narrated:""Allah's Messenger came to a waste area used by people, so he urinated on it while standing. I brought him the (water for) Wudu. Then I left to be away from him, but he called me until I was behind him. So he performed Wudu and wiped (Masaba) over his Khuff"
14,"# Translation of the Hadith\n\n**Qutaybah ibn Sa'īd narrated to us, 'Abdus-Salām ibn Ḥarb al-Mulā'ī narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Anas, who said:**\n\n\The Prophet ﷺ", when he wished to relieve himself," would not raise his garment until he drew close to the ground.\""\n\nAbū 'Īsā [al-Tirmidhī] said: \""Thus Muḥammad ibn Rabī'ah narrated this ḥadīth from al-A'mash", from Anas. And Wakī' and Abū Yaḥyā al-Ḥimmānī narrated from al-A'mash, who said: 'Ibn 'Umar said: The Prophet ﷺ, when he wished to relieve himself," would not raise his garment until he drew close to the ground.'\""\n\n\""Both narrations are *mursal* (i.e.", with a broken chain). It is said that al-A'mash did not hear from Anas, nor from any of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ. He did, however, see Anas ibn Mālik and said: 'I saw him praying,"' and he related from him an account concerning prayer.\""\n\n\""Al-A'mash's name is Sulaymān ibn Mihrān", Abū Muḥammad al-Kāhilī, and he was a *mawlā* (freedman) of their tribe. Al-A'mash said: 'My father was a freedman, and Masrūq inherited him (i.e.," his clientage).'\"""""
15,"Abdullah bin Abu Qatadah narrated from his father:\The Prophet prohibited that a man should touch his penis with his right hand"""
16,"It was narrated to us that Hannād informed us, Abū Mu'āwiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrāhīm, from 'Abd al-Raḥmān ibn Yazīd, who said:\n\nIt was said to Salmān (may Allāh be pleased with him): \Your Prophet (ṣallallāhu 'alayhi wa sallam) has taught you everything"," even the matter of defecation?\"" Salmān (may Allāh be pleased with him) replied: \""Indeed", he forbade us from facing the qiblah when urinating or defecating, and from cleaning ourselves with the right hand, or that any of us should clean himself with fewer than three stones," or that we should clean ourselves with dung or a bone.\""\n\nAbū 'Īsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: In this chapter", there are also narrations from 'Ā'ishah, Khuzaymah ibn Thābit, Jābir, and Khallād ibn al-Sā'ib from his father.\n\nAbū 'Īsā further said: The ḥadīth of Salmān in this chapter is a ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ ḥadīth. This is the view of the majority of the scholars from among the Companions of the Prophet (ṣallallāhu 'alayhi wa sallam) and those after them, who held that cleaning with stones is sufficient even if one does not use water, provided it removes the traces of excrement and urine. This is the position of al-Thawrī, Ibn al-Mubārak, al-Shāfi'ī, Aḥmad," and Isḥāq."""
17,"Abdullah said:\Allah's Messenger went out to relieve himself. So he said: 'Bring me tree stones.'\"" He said"""
18,"Abdullah bin Mas'ud narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: \Do not perform Istinja"""
19,"Aishah said:""Encourage your Husbands to clean themselves with water, for I am too shy of them, and Allah's Messenger would do that"
20,Al-Mughirah bin Shu'bah said:I was with the Prophet on a journey. The Prophet had to relieve himself
21,"Abdullah bin Mughaffal narrated that :the Prophet prohibited that a man should urinate in his bathing area. And he said: \It will only cause misgivings.\"" [He said:] There are narrations on This topic from \""a man from among the Companions of the Prophet"""
22,"Abu Hurairah narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: \If it were not that it would be difficult on my nation"""
23,Zaid bin Khalid Al-Juhani said :'I heard Allah's Messenger saying: 'If it were not that it would be difficult on my nation then
24,"Abu Hurairah reported that the :Prophet said: \When on of you awakens in the night"""
25,Rabah bin Abdur-Rahman bin Abi Sufyan bin Huwaitib narrated from his grandmother
26,Rabah Bin Abdur-Rahman bin Abu Sufyan bin Huwaitib narrated :the same from his grandmother the daughter of Sa'eed bin Zaid
27,"Salamah bin Qais narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: \When you perform Wudu then sniff water in the nose and blow it out"""
28,"Abdullah bin Zaid said:\1 saw the Prophet rinse his mouth and sniff water in his nose using one hand"""
29,Hassan bin Bilal said:\1 saw Ammar bin Yasir performing Wudu," so he went through his beard (with his hand). It was said to him\"" - or he said - \""1 said: 'You go through your beard?' He said: 'And what is there to prevent me? Indeed I saw Allah's Messenger going through his beard.'\"""""
30,"Narrated 'Aishah:that Al-Harith bin Hisham asked the Prophet (ﷺ): 'How does the Revelation come to you?' The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Sometimes it comes to me like the ringing of a bell and that is the hardest upon me, and sometimes the angel will appear to me like a man, and he will speak to me such that I understand what he says.'"" 'Aishah said: ""I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) while the Revelation was descending upon him on an extremely cold day. Then it ceased and his forehead was flooded with sweat"
31,Uthman bin Affan narrated that :the Prophet would go through his beard
32,"Abdullah bin Zaid narrated that:\Allah's Messenger wiped over his head with his hands"""
33,"Ar-Rubay' bint Mu'awwidh bin Afra' narrated:\The Prophet wiped his head two times: He began with the rear of his head"""
34,"Ar-Rubayy bint Mu'awidh bin Afra narrated that :she saw the Prophet performing Wudu. She said: \He wiped his head"""
35,"Abdullah bin Zaid narrated that :he saw the Prophet performing Wudu, and that he wiped his head with water that was not left over from his hands"
36,"Ibn 'Abbas narrated:\The Prophet wiped his head and his ears: the outside and the inside of them.\"" ($ahih)"""
37,"Abu Umamah narrated:\The Prophet performed Wudu; so he washed his face three times"""
38,"Asim bin Laqit bin Sabirah narrated from his father that :the Prophet Muhammad said: \When performing Wudu go between the fingers"""
39,"Ibn Abbas narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: \When performing Wudu go between the fingers of your hands and (toes of) your feet"""
40,"Al-Mustawrid bin Shaddad Al-Fihri said :\I saw the Prophet when he was performing Wudu doing that to the toes on his feet with his pinky"""
41,Abu Hurairah narrated that :the Prophet said:   Protect the heels from the Fire!
42,"Narrated Jabir bin Samurah:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) had a wide mouth (Dali' Al-Fam), his eyes were Ashkal, and he had thin heals (Manhus Al-'Aqib)"
43,"Abu Hurairah narrated:\The Prophet performed Wudu two time (for each limb)"""
44,"Narrated Abu Hurairah:""I have not seen anything more beautiful than the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). It was as if the sun flowed upon his face. And I have not seen anyone quicker in his walking than the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). It was as if the earth was made easy for him. We would be exerting ourselves while he would not be struggling"
45,"Isma'il ibn Musa al-Fazari narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Thabit ibn Abi Safiyyah, he said: I asked Abu Ja'far, \Did Jabir narrate to you that the Prophet", peace be blessings be upon him, performed wudu' (ablution) washing each limb once, and twice," and three times?\"" He replied"," \""Yes.\"""""
46,"Abū ʿĪsā said: Wakīʿ narrated this Ḥadīth from Thābit ibn Abī Ṣafiyyah, who said: \I asked Abū Jaʿfar"," 'Did Jābir narrate to you that the Prophet ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam performed wuḍū' once for each limb?' He replied: 'Yes.'\"" \n\nWe were informed of this by Hannād and Qutaybah", both of whom said: Wakīʿ narrated to us from Thābit ibn Abī Ṣafiyyah. \n\nAbū ʿĪsā said: This narration is more authentic (aṣaḥḥ) than the Ḥadīth of Sharīk, because it has been transmitted through multiple chains from Thābit, similar to the narration of Wakīʿ. Sharīk is prone to frequent errors (kathīr al-ghalaṭ)," and Thābit ibn Abī Ṣafiyyah is Abū Ḥamzah al-Thumālī."""
47,"Abdullah bin Zaid narrated that:\The Prophet performed Wudu. So he washed his face three times"""
48,"Abu Hayyah narrated:\I saw Ali performing Wudu. He washed his hands until he cleaned them"""
49,"Narrated to us Qutaybah and Hannad, both saying: narrated to us Abu al-Ahwaz, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd Khayr, who mentioned from Ali a narration similar to the hadith of Abu Hayyah, except that Abd Khayr said: \When he (peace be upon him) completed his ablution"," he would take from the remaining water of his ablution with his palm and drink it.\""\n\nAbu Isa said: The hadith of Ali was narrated by Abu Ishaq al-Hamdani from Abu Hayyah", Abd Khayr, and al-Harith, from Ali (may Allah be pleased with him). And Zaidah ibn Qudamah and others narrated from Khalid ibn Alqamah, from Abd Khayr, from Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), the hadith of ablution in its entirety.\n\nAnd this is a hasan sahih hadith.\n\nHe said: Shu'bah narrated this hadith from Khalid ibn Alqamah, but he erred in his name and his father's name," saying: \""Malik ibn Urfatah\"" from Abd Khayr", from Ali.\n\nHe said: And it was narrated from Abu Awana, from Khalid ibn Alqamah, from Abd Khayr, from Ali.\n\nHe said: And it was narrated from him from Malik ibn Urfatah, similar to the narration of Shu'bah," and the correct version is Khalid ibn Alqamah."""
50,"Abu Hurairah narrated that :the Prophet said: \Jibril came to me and he said: 'O Muhammad! When you perform wudu then perform Nadh"""
51,"Abu Hurairah narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: \Shall I tell you that for which Allah will wipe out your sins"""
52,"And Qutaybah narrated to us, from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad, from al-ʿAlāʾ, a similar narration. Qutaybah said in his hadith: \That is ribāṭ (guarding the frontier in the cause of Allāh)", that is ribāṭ, that is ribāṭ,"\"" repeating it three times. Abū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: In this chapter", there are narrations from ʿAlī, ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr, Ibn ʿAbbās, ʿAbīdah (also called ʿUbaydah ibn ʿAmr), ʿĀʾishah, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿĀish al-Ḥaḍramī, and Anas (may Allāh be pleased with them all). Abū ʿĪsā said: The hadith of Abū Hurayrah (may Allāh be pleased with him) in this chapter is a ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ hadith. Al-ʿAlāʾ ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān is Ibn Yaʿqūb al-Juhanī al-Ḥuraqī," and he is considered trustworthy (thiqah) by the scholars of hadith."""
53,"Aishah narrated:\Allah's Messenger had a cloth that he would use to dry off with after Wudu"""
54,"Muadh bin Jabal narrated:""I saw the Prophet when he performed Wudu, he wiped his face with the edge of his garment."" Abu Eisa said: This Hadith is gharib, and its chain is weak. Rishdin bin Sa'd and Abdur- Rahman bin Ziyad bin An'um Al Ifriqi [narrators in the chain of this Hadith] are weak in Hadith. Some people of knowledge among the Companions of the Prophet and those after them, permitted using a towel after Wudu. Those who disliked it, only disliked it from the view of the saying: ""Wudu is weighed."" That as reported from Sa'eed bin Al- Musayyab and Az-Zuhri. Muhammad bin Humaid [Ar-Razi] narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, he said: Ali bin Mujahid narrated to me, and he is trustworthy to me, from me, from: Tha'labah from Az-Zuhri, he said: ""The towel is only disliked after Wudu because Wudu is weighed"
55,Umar bin Al-Khattab narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: 'Whoever performs Wudu
56,"Safinah narrated:""The Prophet would perform Wudu with a Mudd, and he would perform Ghusl with a Sa"," and he would perform Ghusl with a Sa.\"" حَدَّثَنَا أَحْمَدُ بْنُ مَنِيعٍ، وَعَلِيُّ بْنُ حُجْرٍ، قَالاَ حَدَّثَنَا إِسْمَاعِيلُ ابْنُ عُلَيَّةَ، عَنْ أَبِي رَيْحَانَةَ، عَنْ سَفِينَةَ، أَنَّ النَّبِيَّ صلى الله عليه وسلم كَانَ يَتَوَضَّأُ بِالْمُدِّ وَيَغْتَسِلُ بِالصَّاعِ  . قَالَ وَفِي الْبَابِ عَنْ عَائِشَةَ وَجَابِرٍ وَأَنَسِ بْنِ مَالِكٍ . قَالَ أَبُو عِيسَى حَدِيثُ سَفِينَةَ حَدِيثٌ حَسَنٌ صَحِيحٌ . وَأَبُو رَيْحَانَةَ اسْمُهُ عَبْدُ اللَّهِ بْنُ مَطَرٍ . وَهَكَذَا رَأَى بَعْضُ أَهْلِ الْعِلْمِ الْوُضُوءَ بِالْمُدِّ وَالْغُسْلَ بِالصَّاعِ . وَقَالَ الشَّافِعِيُّ وَأَحْمَدُ وَإِسْحَاقُ لَيْسَ مَعْنَى هَذَا الْحَدِيثِ عَلَى التَّوْقِيتِ أَنَّهُ لاَ يَجُوزُ أَكْثَرُ مِنْهُ وَلاَ أَقَلُّ مِنْهُ وَهُوَ قَدْرُ مَا يَكْفِي ."""
57,"Ubayy bin Ka'b narrated that :the Prophet said: \Indeed there is a Shaitan for Wudu' who is called \""AI-Walahan.\"" So beware of having misgivings about water"""
58,"Anas narrated that :\The Prophet would perform wudu for every Salat"""
59,"It has been related in a narration from Ibn Umar that :the Prophet said: \Whoever performs Wudu while in a state of purity"""
60,"Amr bin Amir Al-Ansari narrated that he heard Anas bin Malik saying:\The Prophet would perform Wudu for every Salat.\"" I said"""
61,"Sulaiman bin Buraidah narrated that his father said:\The Prophet would perform Wudu for every Salat. So during the year of the Conquest"""
62,"Maimunah said:\I and Allah's Messenger would perform Ghusl for Janabah from one vessel"""
63,"Abu Hajib narrated from a man from Banu Ghifar who said:\The Prophet prohibited using the leftover (water) of a woman's Purification"""
64,"A1-Hakim bin Amr AI-Ghifari narrated that:\The Prophet forbade that a man should perform Wudu with the leftover (water) from a woman's purifcation.\"" Or"""
65,"[Ibn Abbas narrated:\One of the wives of the Prophet performed Ghusl with a bowl. Allah's Messenger wanted to perform Wudu with it"""
66,Narrated Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) that it was said:\n\n\O Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), shall we perform wudu' from the well of Buda'ah? It is a well into which menstrual rags, the flesh of dogs," and foul things are thrown.\""\n\nThe Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) replied:\n\n\""Indeed", water is pure," and nothing can render it impure.\""\n\nAbu 'Eesah (i.e.", Imam At-Tirmidhi) said: This is a Hasan hadith. Abu Usamah had transmitted this hadith excellently, for no one transmitted the hadith of Abu Sa'eed regarding the well of Buda'ah more excellently than Abu Usamah. And this hadith has been narrated through other chains from Abu Sa'eed. In this chapter," there are also narrations from Ibn 'Abbas and 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with them both)."""
67,"Ibn Umar narrated:\I heard AlIah's Messenger while he was being asked about water in open areas of the land"""
68,"Abu Hurairah narrated that :the Prophet said: \Let none of you urinate [in still water"""
69,"Abu Hurairah narrated:\A man asked Allah's Messenger 'O Messenger of Allah! We sail the seas"""
70,"Ibn Abbas narrated:\The Prophet passed by two graves. He said: 'These two are being punished. And they are not being punished for something major. As for this one"""
71,"Umm Qais bin Mihsan narrated:\I entered upon the Prophet with a son of mine who was not yet eating food. He urinated on him"""
72,"Anas narrated:""Some people from Urainah arrived in Al-Madinah, and they were uncomfortable (and ill from the climate). So Allah's Messenger sent them some camels from charity. He told them: ""Drink from their milk and urine."" So they killed the camel driver that Allah's Messenger sent, and they violently drove off the camels, and apostatized from Islam. So the Prophet came to them, he cut off their hands and feet on opposite side, and branded their eyes, and threw them in Al-Harrah."" Anas said, ""So I saw one of them working over the ground with his mouth, until they died"
73,"Anas bin Malik narrated:\Allah's Messenger only poked out their eyes because they had poked out the eyes of the camel driver.\"" Abu 'Eisa said: This Hadfth is Gharib. We do not know anyone who mentioned it other than this shaikh"""
74,"Abu Hurairah narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: \There no Wudu except for a sound or a smell"""
75,"Abu Hurairah narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: \When one of you is in the Masjid"""
76,"Abu Hurairah narrated that :the Prophet said: \Indeed Allah does not accept the prayer of one of you when he commits Hadath"""
77,"Narrated by Ismāʿīl ibn Mūsā — a Kūfan — and Hannād and Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd al-Muḥāribī, with the same meaning. They said: ʿAbd al-Salām ibn Ḥarb al-Mulāʾī narrated to us, from Abū Khālid al-Dālānī, from Qatādah, from Abū al-ʿĀliyah, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allāh be pleased with them both), that he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) sleeping while in prostration (sujūd) until he snored or exhaled audibly, then he stood up to pray. So I said, \O Messenger of Allāh"," you have indeed slept.\"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said:\n\n\""Wuḍūʾ is not obligatory except upon one who sleeps lying down (muḍṭajiʿan)", for when one lies down," one's joints become relaxed.\""\n\nAbū ʿĪsā said: And Abū Khālid's name is Yazīd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān.\n\nHe said: And in this chapter there are narrations from ʿĀʾishah (may Allāh be pleased with her)", Ibn Masʿūd (may Allāh be pleased with him)," and Abū Hurayrah (may Allāh be pleased with him)."""
78,"Anas bin Malik narrated:""The companions of Allah's Messenger would sleep, then stand to pray, They would not perform Wudu"
79,"Abu Hurairah narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: \Wudu is (required) from what fire has touched"""
80,"Jabir narrated:\Allah's Messenger went out and I went with him. He entered upon a woman from the Ansar. She slaughtered a sheep and he ate from it; and she brought a basket with ripe dates and he ate from it. Then he performed Wudu for Zuhr and prayed. Then he finished"""
81,"Al-Bara bin Azib narrated:Allah's Messenger was asked about performing Wudu for camel meat. He said: \Perform Wudu for it.\"" He Was asked about Wudu after eating goat meat. So he said: \""Do not perform Wudu for it"""
82,"Busrah bint Safwan narrated that :the Prophet said: \Whoever touches his penis"""
83,Busrah narrated :a similar report (as no. 82) from the Prophet
84,"# Translation of the Hadith Narration\n\n**Abū al-Zinād** narrated this ḥadīth, from **ʿUrwah**, from **Busrah**, from the Prophet ﷺ.\n\n**ʿAlī ibn Ḥujr** related it to us, saying: **ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī al-Zinād** narrated to us, from his father, from **ʿUrwah**, from **Busrah**, from the Prophet ﷺ, with a similar narration.\n\nThis is the position of more than one of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ and the Tābiʿūn. **Al-Awzāʿī**, **Al-Shāfiʿī**, **Aḥmad**, and **Isḥāq** held this opinion.\n\n**Muḥammad** (ibn Ismāʿīl al-Bukhārī) said: \The most authentic narration on this topic is the ḥadīth of **Busrah**.\""\n\n**Abū Zurʿah** (al-Rāzī) said: \""The ḥadīth of **Umm Ḥabībah** on this topic is authentic (ṣaḥīḥ).\"" It is the ḥadīth of **ʿAlāʾ ibn al-Ḥārith**", from **Makḥūl**, from **ʿAnbasah ibn Abī Sufyān**," from **Umm Ḥabībah**.\n\n**Muḥammad** said: \""Makḥūl did not hear directly from **ʿAnbasah ibn Abī Sufyān**; rather"," Makḥūl narrated from **ʿAnbasah** through an intermediary man in other than this ḥadīth.\"" And it was as though he (Muḥammad) did not consider this ḥadīth to be authentic."""
85,"Qais bin Talq bin Ali - [and he is] Al-Hanafi narrated from his father, that:the Prophet said: 'Is it other than a piece of his flesh?"" Or: ""part of him?"
86,
87,"Madan bin Abi Talhah narrated from Abu Ad-Darda that :\Allah's Messenger vomited [so he broke fast] so he performed Wudu.\"" So I met Thawban in a Masjid in Damascus"""
88,"Abdullah bin Mas'ud narrated:\The Prophet asked me: \""What is in your Idawah (water skin)?\"" I said: \""Nabidh.\"" He said: \""Dates are wholesome and water is pure.\"" He said: \""So he performed Wudu with it"""
89,"Ibn Abbas narrated :the Prophet drank milk. Then he called for water to rinse out his mouth. Then he said: \Indeed it has fat.\"" [He said:] There are narrations on this topic from Sahl bin Sa'd As-Sa'idi and Umm Salamah. Abu Eisa said: [And] this Hadith is Hasan Sahih. Some of the people of knowledge held the view that one is to wash the mouth after drinking milk and this is recommended according us. Some others did not hold the view that one is to wash out the mouth after drinking milk"""
90,"# Translation of the Hadith\n\n**Narrated by Naṣr ibn ʿAlī and Muḥammad ibn Bashshār**, both of whom said: **Abū Aḥmad Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Zubayrī** narrated to us, from **Sufyān**, from **al-Ḍaḥḥāk ibn ʿUthmān**, from **Nāfiʿ**, from **Ibn ʿUmar** (may Allāh be pleased with them both), that:\n\n> A man gave salām (greeting of peace) upon the Prophet ﷺ while he was urinating, and he ﷺ did not return the greeting.\n\n**Abū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī)** said: *\This is a ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ hadith. This is considered disliked (makrūh) among us specifically in the context of answering the call of nature — that is"," during the acts of defecation and urination. Some of the people of knowledge have explained this matter. And this is the best narration that has been reported on this topic.\""*\n\n**Abū ʿĪsā** further said: *\""In this chapter", there are narrations from al-Muhājir ibn Qunfudh, ʿAbdullāh ibn Ḥanẓalah, ʿAlqamah ibn al-Faghwāʾ, Jābir," and al-Barāʾ (may Allāh be pleased with them all).\""*\n\n---\n\n**Source:** *Jāmiʿ al-Tirmidhī* — Chapter on the Dislikability of Returning Salām While Relieving Oneself."""
91,"Abu Hurairah narrated that :the Prophet said: \Wash the vessel the dog has drunk from seven times: the first or the last of them with dirt. And when the cat drinks out of it"""
92,"Humaidah bint Ubaid bin Rifa'ah narrated:\Kabshah bint Ka'b bin Malik - she was (married) with Ibn Abi Qatadah - narrated \""That Abu Qatadah visited her"""
93,"# Translation of the Hadith\n\n**Hannād narrated to us, Wakīʿ narrated to us, from al-Aʿmash, from Ibrāhīm, from Hammām ibn al-Ḥārith, who said:**\n\nJarīr ibn ʿAbdullāh (may Allāh be pleased with him) urinated, then performed ablution (*wuḍūʾ*) and wiped over his leather socks (*khuffayn*). It was said to him, \Do you do this?\"" He replied"," \""What should prevent me"," when I have seen the Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him) do it?\""\n\nIbrāhīm said: \""The Ḥadīth of Jarīr used to please them"," because his acceptance of Islām occurred after the revelation of Sūrat al-Māʾidah.\""\n\nThis is the statement of Ibrāhīm"," meaning that it used to please them.\n\nHe said: \""And in this chapter (there are narrations) from ʿUmar", ʿAlī, Ḥudhayfah, al-Mughīrah, Bilāl, Saʿd, Abū Ayyūb, Salmān, Burayrah, ʿAmr ibn Umayyah, Anas, Sahl ibn Saʿd, Yaʿlā ibn Murrah, ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmiṭ, Usāmah ibn Sharīk, Abū Umāmah, Jābir, Usāmah ibn Zayd," Ibn ʿUbādah — and it is also said Ibn ʿImārah — and Ubayy ibn ʿImārah.\""\n\nAbū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: \""The Ḥadīth of Jarīr is a *ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ* (good and authentic) Ḥadīth.\""\n\n---\n\n**Note:** This Ḥadīth", narrated by Jarīr ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Bajalī (may Allāh be pleased with him), is recorded in *Sunan al-Tirmidhī* and serves as a foundational proof for the permissibility of wiping over leather socks (*al-masḥ ʿalā al-khuffayn*) during ablution. Its particular significance, as noted by Ibrāhīm al-Nakhaʿī," lies in the fact that Jarīr's conversion to Islām took place after the revelation of Sūrat al-Māʾidah — which contains the verse of ablution (5:6) — thereby demonstrating that the practice of wiping over the *khuffayn* was established and observed by the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) after that revelation."""
94,"It has been related from Sahr bin Hawshah that he said:\I saw Jarir bin 'Abdullah performing Wudu and he wiped over his Khuff. I asked him about that. He replied"""
95,"Khuzaimah bin Thabit narrated:\The Prophet was asked about wiping over the Khuff. So he said: \""Three (days) for the traveler"""
96,"# Translation of the Hadith\n\n**Hannād narrated to us:** Abū al-Ahwāṣ narrated to us, from ʿĀṣim ibn Abī al-Najūd, from Zirr ibn Ḥubaysh, from Ṣafwān ibn ʿAssāl رضي الله عنه, who said:\n\n\The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to command us", when we were on a journey, not to remove our leather socks for three days and their nights, except in the case of major ritual impurity (janābah), but not on account of defecation, urination," or sleep.\""\n\nAbū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: **\""This is a ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ hadith.\""**\n\nHe further stated: \""Al-Ḥakam ibn ʿUṭaybah and Ḥammād narrated from Ibrāhīm al-Nakhaʿī", from Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Jadalī, from Khuzaymah ibn Thābit," but this chain is not authentic (lā yaṣiḥḥ).\""\n\nʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī said: Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd reported that Shuʿbah said: **\""Ibrāhīm al-Nakhaʿī did not hear the hadith of wiping (al-masḥ) from Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Jadalī.\""**\n\nZāʾidah said"," from Manṣūr: \""We were in the chamber of Ibrāhīm al-Taymī", and Ibrāhīm al-Nakhaʿī was with us. Ibrāhīm al-Taymī narrated to us from ʿAmr ibn Maymūn, from Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Jadalī, from Khuzaymah ibn Thābit, from the Prophet ﷺ," regarding wiping over the leather socks.\""\n\nMuḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl (al-Bukhārī) said: **\""The best narration on this topic is the hadith of Ṣafwān ibn ʿAssāl al-Murādī.\""**\n\nAbū ʿĪsā said: **\""And this is the position of the majority of scholars from among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ", the Tābiʿūn, and those after them among the jurists, such as Sufyān al-Thawrī, Ibn al-Mubārak, al-Shāfiʿī, Aḥmad, and Isḥāq. They said: 'The resident wipes for one day and one night," and the traveller wipes for three days and their nights.'\""**\n\nAbū ʿĪsā further said: **\""It has been narrated from some of the people of knowledge that they did not stipulate a time limit for wiping over the leather socks"," and this is the position of Mālik ibn Anas.\""**\n\nAbū ʿĪsā then affirmed: **\""And the stipulation of a time limit (al-taqwīt) is more authentic.\""**\n\nHe also noted: **\""This hadith has also been narrated from Ṣafwān ibn ʿAssāl through chains other than that of ʿĀṣim.\""**\n\n---\n\n*This hadith establishes the permissibility of wiping over leather socks (al-khuffayn) during travel for a period of three days and nights", and one day and night for the resident, with the exception of major ritual impurity (janābah)," which necessitates removal and full ritual bathing (ghusl).*"""
97,"AI-Mughirah bin Shu'bah narrated:\The Prophet wiped over the Khuff and its bottom"""
98,"AI-Mughirah bin Shu'bah narrated:\I saw the Prophet wiping over the Khuff: on the tops of them"""
99,"Al-Mughirah bin Shu`bah narrated:\The Prophet performed Wudu' and wiped over his socks and sandals"""
100,"Ibn Al-Mughirah bin Shu'bah narrated from his father:\The Prophet performed Wudu and wiped over the Khuff and 'Imamah.\"" Abu Bakr (one of the narrators) said: \""And indeed I heard it from Ibn Al Mughirah"""
101,"BilaI narrated:\The Prophet wiped over the Khuff and the Khimar"""
102,"Abu Ubaidah bin Muttammad bin Ammar bin Yasir said:\I asked Jabir bin Abdullah about wiping over the Khuff. He said"""
103,"Ibn 'Abbas narrated that his maternal aunt Maimunah said:\I prepared some water for the Prophet to perform Ghusl for Janabah with. So he turned the vessel with his left hand"""
104,"Aishah narrated:""When AlIah's Messenger wanted to perform Ghusl for Janabah, he would begin by washing his hands before putting them into the vessel. Then he would wash his private area, and perform the Wudu (as one does) for Salat. Then he would wet his hair with the water, then he would pour water over his head with his hands three times"
105,"Umm Salamah narrated :\I said: 'O Messenger of Allah! I am woman with tight braids on my head"""
106,"Abu Hurairah narrated that :the Prophet said: \Under every hair is sexual impurity so wash (all of) the hair and cleanse the skin"""
107,"Aishah narrated:\The Prophet would not perform Wudu after the Ghusl"""
108,"**Narration from 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her):**\n\nAbu Musa Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us — al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us — from al-Awza'i — from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim — from his father — from 'Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said:\n\n*\When the circumcised part passes the circumcised part"," then the ritual bath (ghusl) becomes obligatory.\""* She said: *\""I performed it", and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) also performed it," and we both took the ritual bath.\""*\n\nHe (the compiler) further stated: *\""In this chapter", there are also narrations from Abu Hurayrah, 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr," and Rafi' ibn Khadij (may Allah be pleased with them).\""*"""
109,"Aishah narrated that :the Prophet said: \When the circumcised meets the circumcised then Ghusl is required"""
110,"Narrated Ubayy ibn Ka'b, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: \Indeed", the emission of water (madhi) necessitating ghusl was a concession (rukhsah) in the early days of Islam," but it was later prohibited (nuhiya 'anha).\"""""
111,Ma'mar narrated :a similar narration (as Hadith no. 110) from
112,"Narrated Al-Bara bin 'Azib:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said to 'Ali bin Abi Talib: ""You are from me, and I am from you."" And there is a story along with this Hadith"
113,"Aishah narrated:\The Prophet was asked about a man who finds wetness and he does not remember having a wet dream. So he said: 'He is to perform Ghusl. And (he was asked) about a man who had a wet dream but does not find any wetness"""
114,"Ali narrated:\I asked the Prophet about Al-Madhi. He said: \""For Al-Madhi is Wudu"""
115,"Sahl bin Hunaif said:\I suffered from a severe and troubling case of Al-Madhi. I was performing Ghusl often because of it. So I mentioned that to Allah's Messenger and asked him about it. He said: \""You only need to perform Wudu for that.\"" I said: \""O Messenger of Allah! How about when it gets on my clothes?\"" He said: \""It is sufficient for you to take a handful of water and sprinkle it n your garment wherever you see that it has touched it"""
116,"Hammam bin AI-Harith narrated:\Aishah had a guest to whom she lent a yellow wrap for him to sleep in. He had a wet dream"""
117,"# Translation of the Hadith\n\n**Narrated by Ahmad ibn Mani', who said:** Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Maymun ibn Mihran, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from 'Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), that she washed semen from the garment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him).\n\nAbu 'Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: **\This is a hasan sahih hadith.\""**\n\nHe further stated: **\""There are narrations on this topic from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him).\""**\n\nHe then clarified: **\""The hadith of 'Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) regarding her washing semen from the garment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) does not contradict the hadith concerning rubbing (al-fark)", for although rubbing may suffice," it is nonetheless recommended (mustahabb) for a person that no trace of it be seen upon his garment.\""**\n\nIbn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: **\""Semen is of the same status as nasal mucus; therefore", remove it from yourself," even if it be with a piece of idhkhir (fragrant rush) grass.\""**\n\n---\n\n*Note: This hadith is recorded in Sunan al-Tirmidhi and addresses the jurisprudential ruling (hukm) regarding the removal of semen (mani) from clothing", establishing it as something that should be washed off," while also noting the scholarly discussion on whether rubbing alone suffices or washing is preferred.*"""
118,"Aishah narrated:\Allah's Messenger would sleep while he was Junub"""
119,Abu Ishaq:There is a similar report (as no. 1I8) narrated via Abu Ishaq
120,"Umar narrated that :he asked the Prophet: \Can one of us sleep while he is Junub?\"" So he replied: \""Yes"""
121,"Abu Hurairah narrated that :the Prophet met him while he was Junub. He said: \[So I slipped away from him - meaning:] I withdrew - to perform Ghusl. Then he returned"""
122,Umm Salamah narrated:Umm Sulaim bint Milhan came to the Prophet and she said: 'O Messenger of Allah! Indeed Allah is not embarrassed of the truth. So is it required of a woman - meaning Ghusl - when she sees in her sleep similar to what a man sees?' He replied: 'Yes. When she finds water (wetness)
123,"Aishah narrated:\Sometimes the Prophet would perform Ghusl from Janabah then come to seek warmth from me"""
124,"Abu Dharr narrated that :AlIah's Messenger said: \Pure clean earth is a purifier for the Muslim; even if he did not find water for ten years. Then if he finds water"""
125,"Aishah narrated:\Fatimah bint Abi-Hubaish came to the Prophet and said: 'O Messenger of Allah! I am a woman who suffers from persistent bleeding and I do not become clean. Shall I give up Salat?' He said: 'No. That is only a bIood vessel"""
126,"Qutaybah narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu al-Yaqzan, from Adi ibn Thabit, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace be upon him), that he said regarding the woman experiencing istihadah (irregular vaginal bleeding): \She should abstain from prayer during the days of her usual menstrual period", in which she previously menstruated. Then she should perform ghusl (full ritual bath), and make wudu (ablution) for every prayer," and she should fast and pray.\"""""
127,"A similar narration as no. 120. :Abu Eisa said: Sharik is alone in narrating this Hadith from Abu Al Yaqzan.[He said:] I asked Muhammad (ibn Isma'il AI-Bukhari) about this Hadlth. I said: \Adiyy bin Thabit from his father"""
128,"Hamnah bint Jahsh narrated:\I had a case of blood flow that was severe and excessive. So I went to the Prophet to inform him and ask him about it. I found him in the house of my sister Zainab bint Jahsh. I said"""
129,"Aishah narrated:\Umm Habibah hint Jahsh sought a verdict from Allah's Messenger. She said 'I suffer from persistent bleeding such that I do not become pere. Shall I give up the Salat?' He said: 'No"""
130,"Mu'adhah narrated that :a woman asked Aishah: \Shouldn't one of us make up her prayers the days of her menstruation?\"" So she said"""
131,"Ibn Umar narrated that :the Prophet said: \The menstruating woman does not recite - nor the Junub - anything from the Qur'an.\"" [He said:] There is narration on this topic from Ali"""
132,"# Translation of the Hadith\n\n**Bundār narrated to us:** ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī narrated to us, from Sufyān, from Manṣūr, from Ibrāhīm, from al-Aswad, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said:\n\n\The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would", when I was menstruating, command me to wrap a waist-wrapper (izār)," and then he would embrace me intimately (without full sexual relations).\""\n\nHe (Abū ʿĪsā) said: \""There are narrations on this topic from Umm Salamah and Maymūnah (may Allah be pleased with them).\""\n\nAbū ʿĪsā said: \""The Ḥadīth of ʿĀʾishah is a ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ ḥadīth. This is the position of more than one scholar among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and the Tābiʿūn", and this is the view held by al-Shāfiʿī, Aḥmad," and Isḥāq.\"""""
133,"Abdullah bin Sa'd narrated:I asked the Prophet about eating with a menstruating woman. He said: \Eat with her"""
134,"Aishah narrated:\Allah's Messenger said to me: 'Bring me the Khumrah from the Masjid.' She said: \""I said: 'I am menstruating.' He said: 'Indeed your menstruation is not in your hand"""
135,"Abu Hurairah narrated that :the Prophet said: \Whoever engages in sexual intercourse with a menstruating woman"""
136,"Ibn Abbas narrated that :the Prophet said about a man who had sexual intercourse with his wife while she is menstruating: \He should give half a Dinar in charity"""
137,"Ibn Abbas narrated that :the Prophet said: \When the blood is red then (give) a Dinar. And when the blood is yellow then half Dinar"""
138,"Asma' bint Abu Bakr narrated that :a woman asked the Prophet about a garment that was touched by some menstrual blood. So Allah's Messenger said: \Remove it"""
139,"Umm Salamah narrated:\The time of waiting for Nifas during the time of AIlah's Messenger was forty days. We used to cover our faces with reddish-brown Wars"""
140,"Narrated 'Abdullah bin Az-Zubair:from Az-Zubair, who said: ""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) gathered together his parents for me the Day of Quraizah, (i.e. the battle of Ahzab) and said: 'May my mother and father be ransomed for you"
141,Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri narrated that :the Prophet said: When one of you comes to his wife
142,"# Translation of the Hadith\n\n**It was narrated to us** that Hannād ibn al-Sarī said: It was narrated to us that Abū Mu'āwiyah narrated from Hishām ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from 'Abdullāh ibn al-Arqam, who said:\n\nThe prayer was about to commence, so he took a man by the hand and placed him forward to lead the prayer, as he was the imām of his people. He then said: **\I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'When the prayer is established and one of you finds the need to relieve himself"," let him begin with relieving himself.'\""**\n\nHe said: **And in this chapter there are narrations from 'Ā'ishah", Abū Hurayrah, Thawbān, and Abū Umāmah (may Allah be pleased with them).**\n\nAbū 'Īsā said: **The Hadith of 'Abdullāh ibn al-Arqam is a *hasan sahīh* (good and authentic) Hadith.**\n\nThus narrated Mālik ibn Anas, Yahyā ibn Sa'īd al-Qattān, and more than one of the Huffādh (preservers of Hadith) from Hishām ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from 'Abdullāh ibn al-Arqam.\n\nAnd Wahayb and others narrated from Hishām ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from a man, from 'Abdullāh ibn al-Arqam.\n\n**This is the position of more than one of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ and the Tābi'ūn (Successors).**\n\nAhmad and Isḥāq held this view," saying: **\""One should not stand for prayer while experiencing the urge to relieve oneself of stool or urine.\""**\n\nThey further said: **\""If one has already entered the prayer and then feels such an urge"," he should not break off from the prayer so long as it does not occupy his attention.\""**\n\nSome of the scholars of knowledge said: **\""There is no harm in praying while experiencing the urge to pass stool or urine"," so long as it does not distract him from his prayer.\""**\n\n---\n\n*This Hadith is recorded in Jāmi' al-Tirmidhī and establishes the principle of prioritizing the removal of distraction before commencing the prayer"," in order to achieve proper khushū' (devotion and concentration) in salāh.*"""
143,"Narrated to us by Abū Rajāʾ, Qutaybah, narrated to us by Mālik ibn Anas, from Muḥammad ibn ʿUmarah, from Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm, from the *umm walad* (freed slave woman) of ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf, who said: \I said to Umm Salamah: 'I am a woman who lengthens her garment and walks in filthy places.' She said: 'The Messenger of Allah", peace and blessings be upon him," said: **\""What comes after it purifies it.\""**'\""\n\nHe (the narrator) said: \""And in this chapter (there is also a narration) from ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd", who said: 'We were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him," and we would not perform ablution (*wuḍūʾ*) from stepping on filth.'\""\n\nAbū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: \""And this is the view of more than one scholar of knowledge. They said: 'If a man steps on a filthy place", it is not obligatory for him to wash his foot unless it is wet," in which case he should wash what has been affected.'\""\n\nAbū ʿĪsā said: \""And ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Mubārak narrated this ḥadīth from Mālik ibn Anas", from Muḥammad ibn ʿUmarah, from Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm, from the *umm walad* of Hūd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf, from Umm Salamah. However, this is an error (*wahm*), for ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf did not have a son named Hūd. Rather, it is from the *umm walad* of Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf," from Umm Salamah. And this is the correct version (*ṣaḥīḥ*).\"""""
144,
145,"Ikrimah narrated that :Ibn Abbas was asked ahout Tayammum. He said: \When Allah mentioned Wudu in His Book"""
146,"Ali narrated:\Allah's Messenger would recite the Qur'an in all conditions"""
147,"Abu Hurairah narrated:\A Bedouin entered the Masjid while the Prophet was sitting. He prayed"""
148,Anas bin Malik narrated similar to this (no. 147).:[He said:] There are narrations on this topic from 'Abdullah bin Mas'ud
